              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Paul Salvatore, petitioners argue that the Second Circuit erred in imposing a blanket ban on collectively bargained forum\u2011selection clauses for arbitration of ADEA claims."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Paul Salvatore",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f775f4efe490-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Paul Salvatore, petitioners contend that Congress, through the NLRA, the Federal Arbitration Act, and Section\u202f301, intended to empower unions to bargain over dispute\u2011resolution methods, including arbitration of statutory claims."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Paul Salvatore",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f775f4efe490-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Paul Salvatore, petitioners assert that the Second Circuit misapplied Alexander\u202fv.\u202fGardner\u2011Denver, a case about claim preclusion, to the issue of enforcing an arbitration agreement for statutory claims."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f775f4efe490-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f775f4efe490-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 17,
              "start": 17
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners maintain that the collective\u2011bargaining agreement at issue gives the union exclusive control over grievance arbitration, leaving no avenue for individual employees to pursue arbitration independently."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "David C. Frederick",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f775f4efe490821cd1f67b9dce8431763035cfd7eb774a5b9cd61921eca73984",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f775f4efe490-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to David C. Frederick, respondents argue that the Second Circuit\u2019s judgment should be affirmed because a collective\u2011bargaining agreement gives the union exclusive control over grievances, unions have inherent conflicts of interest regarding individual anti\u2011discrimination rights, and unions lack authority to serve as gatekeepers of employees\u2019 substantive ADEA rights."
      }
    ],
